            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "meta-google/recipes-phosphor/flash/gbmc-update/40-gbmc-upgrade.sh",
                    "line": 51,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "William A. Kennington III",
                        "email": "wak@google.com",
                        "username": "wak-google"
                    },
                    "message": "You don't need any of the exclude regex stuff if you just did `image-gbmc-[^/.]+$`. We wouldn't want to use any other arbitrary extension either if it gets added. We want the primary image file only."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-google/recipes-phosphor/flash/gbmc-update/40-gbmc-upgrade.sh",
                    "line": 51,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Mo Elbadry",
                        "email": "elbadrym@google.com",
                        "username": "melbadry97"
                    },
                    "message": "I can take it off but I added it as protection, I do not see harm from it and it can be useful. Let me know."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-google/recipes-phosphor/flash/gbmc-update/40-gbmc-upgrade.sh",
                    "line": 51,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "William A. Kennington III",
                        "email": "wak@google.com",
                        "username": "wak-google"
                    },
                    "message": "It's not more protection in this case though. It wouldn't ignore someone adding `/image-gbmc-machine.hash` or `/image-gbmc-machine.meta`. The idea with the previous check was to match with the machine name, `.` and `/` cannot be part of the machine name."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-google/recipes-phosphor/flash/gbmc-update/40-gbmc-upgrade.sh",
                    "line": 51,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "William A. Kennington III",
                        "email": "wak@google.com",
                        "username": "wak-google"
                    },
                    "message": "We can keep the new ignore functionality because it could be useful, but I don't think positively trying to guess what to ignore is helpful here."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-google/recipes-phosphor/flash/gbmc-update/40-gbmc-upgrade.sh",
                    "line": 51,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Mo Elbadry",
                        "email": "elbadrym@google.com",
                        "username": "melbadry97"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged - done."
                }
            ],
